#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# number_digit

#% text
# `number_digit(x, k)` gives the digit of `|x|` at position `k` in base 10 (the place of `10^k`, negative `k` after the point); `number_digit(x, k, b)` uses base `b`; a list of positions gives a list, and a list of numbers gives one such list for each number.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
number_digit(123456, 2)
#% output
#= 4

#% cell
number_digit(12.3456, -1)
#% output
#= 3

#% cell
number_digit(pi, range(2, -2, -1))
#% output
#= [0, 0, 3, 1, 4]

#% cell
number_digit(2/3, range(-1, -3, -1))
#% output
#= [6, 6, 6]

#% cell
number_digit([pi, e, 99352, 11/7], [4, 0, -2])
#% output
#= [[0, 3, 4], [0, 2, 1], [9, 2, 0], [0, 1, 7]]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `integer_digits`, `real_digits`
